# Accessibility Strategy

Baseline accessibility for screens, components, forms, navigation, and feedback states.

## Requirements

- Add semantic labels for icon-only buttons and meaningful images.
- Keep tap targets at least `48px` where practical.
- Support keyboard navigation and keep visible focus states.
- Must not rely on color alone; pair status with icon plus text.
- Keep text readable under font scaling.
- Associate form errors with their fields.
- Must not excessive motion; use simple default transitions.
- Must use design tokens for color and contrast; hard-coded colors are prohibited ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)).
- Reusable accessible components must live in `frontend/lib/shared/`; check the catalog first.
- All user-facing text must be localized with concise clinical terminology.

## Dialogs and states

- Dialogs should trap focus and return focus after closing.
- State views must announce loading, empty, and error messages.

## Acceptance

- Tab order is logical; important actions have labels.
- Contrast is readable in light and dark themes.
- Text scaling does not hide controls.

